# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so everything gitignored has to be repeated
# here or `COPY . .` bakes it into the image.
#
# This file is load-bearing for a CLAIM, not just for build speed: the
# Dockerfile header and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md 1c both state that data_cache/ is
# not baked into the image and must be mounted. Without this file that
# statement was false -- `COPY . .` was copying 5.3 GB of real tissue data,
# 647 MB of run history, and a 618 MB macOS virtualenv into the image.

# --- real data: mounted at runtime, never baked in (this is the claim) ---
data_cache/
.export-drive/
supp.zip

# --- writable runtime state: belongs in a volume, not a layer ---
app/runs/
app/projects/
app/reports/
app/uploads/

# --- host-specific / wrong-platform ---
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- not needed by the server image ---
.git/
.github/
landing-3d/          # the marketing site is a separate Next.js app
archive/             # the retired synthetic-era code
results/             # generated reports and figures
marketing/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
